<item>
            <title>[MAHOUT-378] min support parameter ignored in FPGrowth</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-378</link>
                <project id="12310751" key="MAHOUT">Mahout</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The  minSupport parameter is never read in&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;generateFList(Iterator&amp;lt;Pair&amp;lt;List&amp;lt;A&amp;gt;,Long&amp;gt;&amp;gt; transactions, int minSupport) &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One solution is to drop the parameter, i.e.: &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;generateFList(Iterator&amp;lt;Pair&amp;lt;List&amp;lt;A&amp;gt;,Long&amp;gt;&amp;gt; transactions)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I guess this would do the filtering:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;		List&amp;lt;Pair&amp;lt;A, Long&amp;gt;&amp;gt; fList = new ArrayList&amp;lt;Pair&amp;lt;A, Long&amp;gt;&amp;gt;();&lt;br/&gt;
		for (Entry&amp;lt;A, MutableLong&amp;gt; e : attributeSupport.entrySet()) {&lt;br/&gt;
			if (e.getValue().intValue() &amp;gt;= minSupport) &lt;/p&gt;
{
				fList.add(new Pair&amp;lt;A, Long&amp;gt;(e.getKey(), e.getValue()
						.longValue()));
			}
&lt;p&gt;		}&lt;/p&gt;</description>
